            <ArticleTitle>Intraoperative diaphragmatic plication during coronary artery bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>338-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diaphragmatic paralysis following coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG), while often benign, can sometimes require plication. This paper describes the first reported case of intraoperative (CABG) pulmonary plication for a patient with prior diaphragmatic paralysis.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>(c) 2007 S. Karger AG, Basel.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
